#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0129 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "DISCRIMINATING FIXTURE for finding AD0129-F1, FLIPPED by the M2-P1 ruling (option (a), Fix #302). Same parameter, different subjects: study-wide this is exactly the disagreement the PMDA sheet row 101 describes - one BASEC, two BASE, one parameter - and it was SILENT while the Check partitioned by within=[USUBJID, PARAMCD], because the two rows fell in different partitions and each saw a single dependent. With within=PARAMCD the two rows share one partition, key NORMAL carries {120, 130}, and D.13's flag-every-populated-row contract fires BOTH. The file was authored as expect=noViolation with the flip and its pins named in its own note; this is that flip, not a re-aiming. Cross-read with PMDA-AD0130-invalid_cross_subject_disagreement-ADLBC, the mirror. Do NOT propagate to CDISC-AD0129/0130/0732/0733/0693/0694: their own sheet cells say 'for a subject'."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 PARAMCD=SYSBP BASE=120 BASEC=NORMAL
#expectViolationAt row=2 PARAMCD=SYSBP BASE=130 BASEC=NORMAL
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col BASE    type=Num
col BASEC   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | SYSBP | 120 | NORMAL
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | SYSBP | 130 | NORMAL
